From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:06:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(r64): the q5_K MMVQ route lands - proof, null control,
 registry rows

Step 0(a) trace, 0(b) three-shape table, every proof gate, and the finding
that reframes the lane's own headline number.

GATES: targeted MUL_MAT 160 cases x 3 modes 0 FAIL, counts equal across arms;
full MUL_MAT sweep 0 FAIL both arms (the R49-class m=248320 failures did not
appear on this tree); planted RED under DATA_A_Q5_K && NUM_COLS>1 reddens 35
cases with route and 0 with legacy, restored with an empty git diff, re-green
0 FAIL; 27B text 6/6 token-identical on 3 greedy prompts x 2 Q4_K_XL files.

THE NULL CONTROL, and why it is in the report rather than the drawer: with the
shipped n>=5 lever, `route` at n=1..4 is the SAME code path as `default`, and
it still read 0.942 at n=4. Three legacy arms in the same three slots bound
the slot artifact at 1-3%, so that cell is noise-dominated - which means take
1's "n=3/n=4 loss" is NOT established, and n>=5 is the CONSERVATIVE bound
justified by row geometry, not a threshold fitted to a measured loss. The
n=5..8 wins (+5.6% to +20.4%, 5-6 of 6 rounds, both takes) are far outside
that band and survive it.

Also recorded against the lane's convenience: the text cells decode at n=1
where this rule is inert by construction, so they are a no-regression receipt
and NOT evidence about the routed arithmetic; PPL (the R48b ship rule's other
half) is NOT RUN and is owed before any default moves; q6_K is declined as
overfitting.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-252 R64 q5_K MMVQ route, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: op-level perf-mode only (rows in receipts); served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - HQ pairs quiet
Lane: lane-252
Cherry-picked-from: f418e981e (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 1b6185951 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from b37f192e8)
